# Project Architecture

This is a full-stack study abroad agency platform, not a simple MVP.

Use:
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- Supabase Auth
- Supabase Postgres
- Supabase Storage
- Resend
- Vercel deployment

Main modules:
- Public SEO website
- Country pages
- University and course directory
- Scholarship finder
- Eligibility checker
- Cost calculator
- Lead CRM
- Student authentication
- Student dashboard
- Application tracker
- Document upload
- Admin dashboard
- Counselor dashboard
- Email notifications

Rules:
- Use scalable folder structure.
- Use route groups for public, student, admin, and counselor sections.
- Keep business logic in lib/server or service files.
- Keep UI components reusable.
- Never mix admin logic inside public components.
- Never expose Supabase service role key to client components.
- Prefer server components unless client interactivity is required.
- Use server actions or route handlers for mutations.
- Validate all incoming data with Zod.
- Always think about role-based access control.
